{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2174-05-01 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Patel. I’ve reviewed your chart. You came in today because of exhaustion and heavy sweating—can you tell me more about that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2174-05-01 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it started about a week ago. I woke up drenched in sweat, even though I wasn’t hot. It’s been happening every day since."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2174-05-01 15:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And you mentioned feeling completely wiped out—how long have you been feeling that way?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2174-05-01 15:04:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "About three days. I slept 17 hours straight the other night and still felt exhausted."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2174-05-01 15:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You’ve also been on Humira, azathioprine, and prednisone for your psoriatic arthritis and IBD. Did your symptoms start around the time of your last Humira dose?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2174-05-01 15:06:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Now that you mention it—yes, the sweating started the morning after my last injection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2174-05-01 15:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s important. Given your immunosuppression, we’re concerned about infection, but also possible side effects from your medications. We’ll run some tests."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2174-05-01 15:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t had a fever, though. My temperature usually runs low—around 96.3."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2174-05-01 15:09:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s noted. We’ll still check for infections like CMV, EBV, and others. We’ve already done blood work and a chest X-ray—both were normal so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2174-05-01 15:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ve also been having more joint pain in the mornings—worse than usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2174-05-01 15:12:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s part of what we’re monitoring. We’ll keep you on prednisone for now. We’ve held your Humira and azathioprine temporarily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2174-05-01 15:13:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I stop them completely?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2174-05-01 15:14:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. We’re waiting on more test results. If we confirm this is a reaction to Humira, we may discontinue it permanently."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2174-05-02 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your CMV and EBV tests came back negative. Blood cultures show no growth so far. That’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2174-05-02 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. What about the calf pain I’ve been having?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2174-05-02 09:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did an ultrasound—no sign of a blood clot. But we noticed a red, tender lump on your right calf. Dermatology thinks it might be erythema nodosum."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2174-05-02 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What’s that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2174-05-02 09:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s an inflammatory condition, often linked to autoimmune diseases like yours. We’ll biopsy it to confirm, but it’s not an infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2174-05-02 09:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it go away?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2174-05-02 09:07:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Usually, yes—especially once we manage the underlying trigger. We’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2174-05-03 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve completed a CT scan of your chest, abdomen, and pelvis. No signs of infection or cancer. Your liver shows fatty infiltration, which we already knew about."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2174-05-03 10:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So nothing’s showing up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2174-05-03 10:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nothing concerning. Your symptoms are likely related to your immune system—possibly a reaction to Humira. We’re leaning toward stopping it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2174-05-03 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve also been nauseous after meals—could that be related?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2174-05-03 10:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. With your IBD history and family background, we’re watching that. But it’s likely stable—nothing acute."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2174-05-04 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your urine culture and fungal tests are back—no infection. Toxoplasmosis and mycoplasma were negative too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2174-05-04 14:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the pending ones—Aspergillus, coccidioides?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2174-05-04 14:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Still pending, but given your negative CT and blood work, the chance of those is very low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2174-05-05 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did another CT of your neck—no signs of infection or swelling. The old sialocele is still there, but not infected."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2174-05-05 11:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my headaches—they’ve been worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2174-05-05 11:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know. You were supposed to get Botox, but we held off because we needed to rule out infection first. Botox can cause side effects that mimic illness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2174-05-05 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what can we do now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2174-05-05 11:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll consult pain management. They may offer trigger point injections instead."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2174-05-06 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your spinal tap came back clean. No infection in the spinal fluid. That’s a big relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2174-05-06 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the MRI?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2174-05-06 08:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No tumors, strokes, or inflammation. Just some old, stable white matter changes—nothing new."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2174-05-06 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So still no explanation for the headaches?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2174-05-06 08:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not from the scan. But given your history, it’s likely part of your chronic condition. Pain service will see you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2174-05-06 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The biopsy of your calf lesion showed no infection—no bacteria or fungi. Dermatology confirms it’s consistent with erythema nodosum."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2174-05-06 13:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2174-05-06 13:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not dangerous, but it’s a sign your body is inflamed. We’ll restart azathioprine and keep you on prednisone. Humira will be stopped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2174-05-06 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my headaches?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2174-05-06 13:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Pain service gave you trigger point injections with bupivacaine—no steroid, to avoid confusion with infection symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2174-05-06 13:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "How long will that help?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2174-05-06 13:07:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It should last a few days to weeks. You’ll follow up with them as an outpatient."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2174-05-07 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been afebrile, stable, and improving. We’re discharging you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2174-05-07 10:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What meds should I take?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2174-05-07 10:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue prednisone and azathioprine. Stop Humira and Bactrim. We’ve adjusted your morphine and lisinopril doses."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2174-05-07 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the pending tests?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2174-05-07 10:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "A few serologies are still pending. Dermatology will call you with biopsy results. Follow up with rheumatology in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2174-05-07 10:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "If I start feeling worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2174-05-07 10:07:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call your PCP or come back to the ER if you develop fever, worsening pain, or new symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2174-05-07 10:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2174-05-07 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Get some rest, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2174-05-01 14:43:00",
    "admission_end": "2174-05-07 16:54:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 50-year-old male with psoriatic arthritis and undifferentiated IBD, on long-term immunosuppression with Humira, azathioprine, and prednisone, was admitted for one week of profuse sweating and three days of severe exhaustion. Despite being afebrile, his immunocompromised status prompted an extensive infectious workup, including blood cultures, serologies, lumbar puncture, and imaging (CT chest/abdomen/pelvis, MRI brain), all of which were unremarkable. A right calf lesion was biopsied and found consistent with erythema nodosum, with no evidence of infection. Given the temporal association of symptom onset with his last Humira dose, the medication was discontinued. Azathioprine was held during admission but resumed at discharge, along with prednisone. Trigger point injections were administered for worsening cervical headaches, as Botox was deferred due to diagnostic uncertainty. The patient improved clinically, remained stable, and was discharged home with follow-up arranged in rheumatology and dermatology.",
    "problems": [
      "Other malaise and fatigue",
      "Psoriatic arthropathy",
      "Erythema nodosum",
      "Generalized hyperhidrosis",
      "Long-term (current) use of steroids",
      "Abdominal pain, unspecified site",
      "Headache",
      "Other and unspecified noninfectious gastroenteritis and colitis",
      "Secondary diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, not stated as uncontrolled, or unspecified",
      "Adrenal cortical steroids causing adverse effects in therapeutic use",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Other chronic nonalcoholic liver disease",
      "Antineoplastic and immunosuppressive drugs causing adverse effects in therapeutic use",
      "Cornea replaced by transplant",
